cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these bounds or this verification code, please cite it."
title: "Kissing numbers: new lower bounds in dimensions 25 through 96, with verification packages"
abstract: >-
  Verification packages for new lower bounds on the kissing number in 47
  dimensions: 25, 27, 38, 39, 49-63, 68-71 and 73-96.  Four ideas carry them.
  (1) Cross-sections of extremal even unimodular lattices, bounded
  by a k-point linear program on the moments that Venkov's theorem supplies,
  with exact rational dual certificates and with translation and lattice-range
  constraints that the design property alone cannot see; dimension 46 comes out
  exact.  (2) The Leech-style "equator + caps + poles" construction, run over
  P_48 and over Nebe's Gamma_72, where the class threshold decides the shape:
  gamma = 1/4 for the Leech lattice and for Gamma_72 lets a cap head be shared
  by a zero-sum triple of directions, while gamma = 1/3 for P_48 admits only an
  antipodal pair, which is worth half as much; in dimension 25 the caps are
  rebuilt as 1006 heads in the lens of a minimal vector, each removing exactly
  its owner (no removal is ever shared, a theorem), which gives 197569.  (3) Explicit large classes found
  by search, about ten times what Caro-Wei guarantees in every lattice tried.
  (4) The Edel-Rains-Sloane chain evaluated where its authors did not: at n_0 = n
  in dimension 39 with the 2026 constant-weight code tables, as the chain
  (n, 15, 2) in dimensions 62 and 63, and as (96, 24, 6, 1) in dimension 96,
  where it reaches 12886999232 and so overtakes the layered construction
  outright.  Its levels above zero are built here rather than cited, and the
  whole chain is checked in coordinates at the two dimensions where it
  reproduces tau(8) = 240 and tau(16) = 4320 exactly.  The
  repository also records, as carefully as the positive results, the mechanisms
  that were pushed to their exact ceiling and should not be retried, and the
  two claims that were withdrawn when better values appeared.  Dimensions 46 and
  47 are recovered rather than claimed: 23766960 is Boyvalenkov-Cherkashin,
  Results Math. 80 (2025), Paper No. 3, and 12309600 is Sun-Wang,
  arXiv:2607.20359.  Both were obtained here independently and are kept because
  reproducing a published count validates the method.  No floating-point
  arithmetic decides anything.
